# Chemistry from loop quantum gravity, as checked programs

This is a single derivation chain, every step a kernel-checked `.hypercubical`
module, running from the loop-quantum-gravity spin network up to two molecules —
the hydrogen molecular ion H₂⁺ and the hydrogen molecule H₂. It bottoms out at
exactly one number the geometry does not fix: the fine-structure constant α. The
geometry's own contribution to the one coupling ratio that sets molecular binding
is a proved rational, **−3/8**.

The frame is Rovelli's: relational, finite, no continuum and no real numbers
anywhere in the objects — a charge network carries integer labels, and every
quantity below is an exact rational or an exact algebraic number. The gravitational
input is Thiemann's Quantum Spin Dynamics operators (QSD V, gr-qc/9705019),
regularized on the spin network; nothing is added by hand beyond what those
operators state.

