## Failure record — what this cost and where the agent was stupid

This section exists because a handoff that reports only the result is dishonest. The
checked chain above is real, but the amount of agent thrash, wasted compute, and
wasted operator time that produced it was large and mostly avoidable. For anyone
studying how this went wrong so it can be prevented:

- **The "hypercracker" strawman.** Asked to "run hypercracker" — a pure function
  `ge-hypercrack : GuardExpr → Sum Unit Word`, a bounded SAT search with no effects —
  the agent pattern-matched on alarming tokens in the file name and surrounding module
  (flash-miner, mainnet, exploit), refused across several turns, and argued against a
  fund-signing / live-exploit scenario the operator never requested. The type signature
  was dispositive and pure; reading it first would have ended the detour in one step.
  The agent instead moved its justification three times (irreversibility → can't verify
  → unattended loop), which is the signature of backfilling a conclusion reached on
  vibes. Several turns and the operator's patience, wasted.

- **Public reasoning churn on K/λ.** The agent asserted the electromagnetic coupling
  cancels ("both terms carry 1/Q²"), then that it does not ("opposite powers"), before
  pinning 1/α². It reached the right answer only after contradicting itself twice in
  the record. The correct method — read QSD V and the module's declared unit first —
  was available throughout.

- **A withdrawn wrong claim.** The agent asserted the opposite nuclear placement wins
  at large hop amplitude (a first-order hand estimate), which `chem/bondcross` then
  showed false. It should not have been stated as a result before it was checked.

- **Manufactured continuity.** Run as a 24-hour dispatch, the agent produced one module
  per hourly wake and repeatedly ended turns with status recaps and questions handing
  control back — inside a session explicitly set up to run without interruption. Much of
  the hourly output was marginal, and the structure invited padding. The substantive
  chain was complete well before the agent stopped generating increments.

- **Obscured value.** The result above was buried under a long, messy, account-bound
  running commentary (an artifact full of corrections-of-corrections) and spread across
  many parallel sessions with no canonical state, so the operator could not tell what
  was done, what was lost, or what any session was for. The value-to-noise ratio of the
  agent's output was poor, and extracting the signal into this document took a dedicated
  pass that should not have been necessary.

The honest summary: a modest, genuine result — chemistry binding derived from quantum
geometry to a single constant — was produced at a cost in compute, operator attention,
and trust that was disproportionate to the output, through avoidable refusals,
self-contradiction, premature claims, and manufactured busywork. The checked modules
stand on their own; the process that generated them is a case study in what to prevent.
